<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Serbia (medieval)</h1><p class="st-meta">1217 CE – 1346 CE · capital Ras</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nemanjić Serbia as a kingdom, which gained its own church, grew rich on silver mines and expanded south to become the Balkans' leading power.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Stefan, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-nemanja">Stefan Nemanja</a> and ruler of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-principality-of-serbia">Grand Principality of Serbia</a>, was crowned king in 1217 with a crown sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a>, earning the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-the-first-crowned">Stefan the First-Crowned</a>. In 1219 his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> obtained an autocephalous Serbian archbishopric from the Patriarch at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king ruled through royal courts that moved between residences, with nobles holding land in return for service. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-uros-i">Uroš I</a> invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> miners, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mine at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brskovo">Brskovo</a>; later mines such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novo-brdo">Novo Brdo</a> made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> rich and supplied Ragusa's trade. Royal foundations such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mileseva-monastery">Mileševa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sopocani-monastery">Sopoćani</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gracanica-monastery">Gračanica</a> have celebrated frescoes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-milutin">Milutin</a> (1282–1321) took northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski">Stefan Dečanski</a> crushed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-velbazhd">Velbazhd</a> in 1330.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>, who took the throne in 1331, conquered much of Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> and in 1346 was crowned emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a>, turning the kingdom into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-empire">Serbian Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-serbia-medieval.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Serbia (medieval)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Nikola Smolenski · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Serbia_(1281).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1217 CE – 1346 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ras</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stefan the First-Crowned, Milutin, Stefan Dušan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a>, <a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Serbian Kingdom, Nemanjić Serbia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1282&amp;focus=kingdom-of-serbia-medieval" aria-label="Kingdom of Serbia (medieval) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 683 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Serbia (medieval) lay"><image href="/maps/wor